 ```
 
+`top(entries, n)` returns, for each month, its `n` most expensive entries
+(most expensive first; ties broken by category):
+
+```python
+from ledger import load, top
+top(load("data/sample.txt"), 2)
+# {'2026-08': [rent 12000.0, groceries 1250.0], '2026-09': [rent 12000.0, books 890.0]}
+```
+
 Run the tests: `python -m pytest -q`
